<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Maximilian I, Holy Roman Emperor</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1459–1519</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Maximilian of Habsburg</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Maximilian I was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> ruler, King of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a> from 1486 and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-emperor">Holy Roman Emperor</a> from 1508 until his death. His marriage to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mary-of-burgundy">Mary of Burgundy</a> in 1477 brought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/low-countries">Low Countries</a> to the Habsburgs, and his children's Spanish marriages prepared his grandson <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-v-holy-roman-emperor">Charles V</a>'s inheritance of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>. He ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tyrol">Tyrol</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/innsbruck">Innsbruck</a>, acquired <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gorizia">Gorizia</a> in 1500, raised loyal lords to higher rank and at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diet-of-worms-1495">Diet of Worms</a> in 1495 attempted reform of the empire.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/maximilian-i-holy-roman-emperor.jpg" alt="Maximilian I, Holy Roman Emperor" width="320" height="392" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Albrecht Dürer · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Albrecht_D%C3%BCrer_-_Portrait_of_Maximilian_I_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
